-- expect: 12:25: this block performs `Count`, an effect answered by a capability: a block passed to a function performs control operations only (#161, E6: not provided)
-- A block that uses an answering capability (SPEC §30): `tick` is a call on the state of the
-- `count` handler, a capability lent to the body of the `with`. A block passed to a function would
-- need the capability passed with it at each call, which is not provided (SPEC §30 *Open*); a
-- block's control operations need nothing passed, since they go to the sites around it by name.
effect Count { fn tick() -> i32 }
handler count(mut n: i32): Count = { tick() = { n = n + 1; n } }

fn twice(f: !(i32 => i32)) -> i32 = f(1) + f(2)

main -> i32 =
  with count(0) { twice(!{ x -> x + tick() }) }
